# Feature Architecture

Prefer small, composable components.

## Screen responsibilities

A screen should:
- compose feature components
- read route parameters
- invoke feature hooks
- coordinate loading/error/empty states
- remain readable

A screen should NOT contain hundreds of lines of business logic.

## Component responsibilities

Reusable UI components should:
- accept typed props
- avoid direct API calls
- avoid importing unrelated product services
- expose meaningful states through props

Example:

```tsx
<PartnerCard
  partner={partner}
  onPress={() => openPartner(partner.id)}
/>
```

Avoid:

```tsx
<PartnerCard />
```

where the component secretly fetches, mutates, navigates, and manages unrelated state.

## Hooks

Use hooks for reusable behavior:

```text
useCurrentUser()
usePartnerDiscovery()
useConversation()
useMessages()
useSendMessage()
useCorrections()
useNotificationPreferences()
```

Hooks should not become giant "everything" hooks.

## API layer

Centralize:
- base URL
- auth headers
- response parsing
- API errors
- retry behavior

Feature APIs should expose typed functions.

## Design system

Prefer shared primitives:

```text
Button
IconButton
Text
Input
Avatar
Badge
Card
Sheet
Modal
Divider
Skeleton
EmptyState
ErrorState
```

Do not create slightly different versions of the same primitive for every screen.
